PyMuPDF (fitz)  -- NOT A DEPENDENCY OF THIS PRODUCT
  Copyright (c) Artifex Software, Inc.
  Licensed under AGPL-3.0, or a commercial licence from Artifex.

  RESOLVED 2026-08-05: Prajnya ships under Apache-2.0. Distributing
  Apache-2.0 code combined with an AGPL library would relicense the whole
  product as AGPL, so PyMuPDF is NOT a dependency of this product and is
  deliberately absent from requirements.txt.

  It remains selectable as an optional local-development backend for its speed
  and exact word boxes. Distributed builds use pypdfium2 (above), which is the
  default. Measured agreement between the two on the benchmark paper is 93-100%
  of words per page, with figure boxes identical.

  All PDF access goes through the PdfBackend interface in src/processing/pdf/,
  and available_backends() reports each backend's licence so an AGPL fallback
  cannot happen silently. See CLAUDE.md, "The Licence Rule".

